## 4. Non-Goals (Out of Scope)

The following features are **explicitly deferred** unless required by mockups:

- **Tags/Categories system**: Requires new model, join table, complex UI — defer to Phase 2
- **Onboarding flow**: No mockup provided — not in scope
- **Profile picture upload**: No mockup shows this — not in scope
- **Real-time collaboration**: Out of scope for this integration
- **Note colors/backgrounds**: Only if shown in editor mockup
- **Export to PDF/Markdown**: Not in scope
- **Folder organization**: Not in scope

---

## 5. Risks & Mitigations

| Risk | Impact | Mitigation |
|------|--------|------------|
| **FlutterQuill layout conflicts** | Editor UI breaks when restyled | Keep Quill wrapper minimal; style container only, not internal Quill widgets; test on multiple screen sizes |
| **Sync conflicts (Firestore vs sqflite)** | Data loss or duplicates | Use `lastModified` timestamp for conflict resolution; server-wins policy; log conflicts for debugging |
| **DB migration failure** | App crashes on upgrade | Wrap migration in try-catch; provide fallback to keep old schema; test migration on real devices before release |
| **Mixed state management (Bloc + Provider)** | Confusing data flow; race conditions | Keep clear boundaries: AuthBloc for auth only, ThemeNotifier for theme only; document in README which manages what |
| **Offline-first sync edge cases** | Notes stuck in dirty state | Show sync status indicator; allow manual retry; handle connectivity_plus events reliably |

---

## Optional Phase 2 (Post-Integration)

These are **not required** for the initial integration but recommended for future:

- **Feature-first restructure**: Move to `lib/features/{auth,notes,settings}/ui/` pattern for better scalability
- **GetIt dependency injection**: Register Blocs/Cubits via service locator instead of inline `BlocProvider`
- **Tags system**: Add `tags` table, many-to-many relationship, tag picker UI
- **Onboarding carousel**: First-launch experience with shared_preferences flag
- **go_router migration**: Replace `MaterialApp.routes` with declarative routing
